{{also|Scheinen}}
==German==

===Etymology===
{{dercat|de|gem-pro|inh=1}}
From {{inh|de|gmh|schīnen}}, from {{inh|de|goh|skīnan}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*skīnan}}.

Cognate with {{cog|nds-de|schienen}}, {{cog|nl|schijnen}}, {{cog|en|shine}}, {{cog|da|skinne}}, {{cog|eo|ŝajni}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ʃaɪnən/}}
* {{hyphenation|de|schei|nen}}
* {{audio|de|De-scheinen.ogg|a=Germany}}
* {{audio|de|De-at-scheinen.ogg|a=Austria}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb|scheinen<schien,geschienen>}}

# to [[shine]]; to [[gleam]]
#* {{quote-book|de|year=2002|author=w:Peter Bichsel|title=Eisenbahnfahren|publisher=Insel Verlag|year_published=2015|page=12
|passage=Wenn man aus der Kirche kommt, schneit es, oder es regnet, oder die Sonne '''scheint'''.|t=When you come out of the church, it's snowing, or it's raining, or the sun's shining.}}
# {{lb|de|copulative}} to [[seem]]; to [[appear]]; to [[look]]
#: {{ux|de|Es '''scheint''' mir, dass …|It '''seems''' to me that …}}
#: {{ux|de|Du '''scheinst''' erschöpft.|You '''seem''' exhausted.}}

